CVPR,cs_conf,other,Zhu_Unlocking_Positive_Transfer_in_Incrementally_Learning_Surgical_Ins,1,unclassified,1,0,"(a) Prior works learn each instrument prompt in- dependently. (b,c) They overlook the power of positive for- ward and backward transfer between early-acquired and newly- acquired knowledge. (d) In contrast, our work organizes instru- ment prompts from general to specific as a hierarchical prompt parsing tree. (e) It supports positive forward transfer by helping new instrument prompts inherit profitable knowledge from the past to assist new-class learning. (f) It further enables positive back- ward transfer by letting the newly-acquired knowledge wisely re- fine early-acquired knowledge to impr"
CVPR,cs_conf,other,Zhu_Unlocking_Positive_Transfer_in_Incrementally_Learning_Surgical_Ins,2,overview,0,0,"Overview of our self-reflection hierarchical prompt framework. We progressively append instrument-aware prompts into a pre- trained model during the training lifespan. For each new class, before diving into learning its specific prompts, we first build a hierarchical prompt parsing tree to discover the profitable knowledge it could inherit from the past, i.e., the instrument-shared (IS) and n-part-shared knowledge, promoting new-class learning by positive forward knowledge transfer. Simply learning one instrument-distinct (ID) prompt partition would be sufficient to delineate its contour. Base"
