CVPR,cs_conf,medical,Zhang_Contrastive_Cross-Bag_Augmentation_for_Multiple_Instance_Learnin,2,embedding,0,0,"C2Aug consists of: 1) Cross-Bag Augmentation adopts three augmentations to generate two different pseudo-bags from the same input bag, which are then fed into the teacher and student MIL models, respectively. 2) Bag-Level Contrastive Learning computes the bag-level contrastive loss Lbag to bring bag representations with similar features closer in the embedding space. The parameters of the teacher model are updated using exponential moving average (EMA). 3) Group-level Contrastive Learning assigns each instance to a learnable prototype, performs size alignment by compressing the instances towar"
