ICCV,cs_conf,vlm,Anshul_Intra-modal_and_Cross-modal_Synchronization_for_Audio-visual_De,1,curves,1,0,"Synchronization pretraining: (a) We extract video and audio encoding from the input and compute synchronization scores within individual modalities and across modalities. During training, we compute MSE loss with Gaussian targets. (b) The individual synchronization model uses an attention model to compute the temporal alignment between different segment pairs from the primary and secondary input. Here, τ = 15. The scores of the individual pairs are concatenated to create the output feature vector. (a) Decoder Variant (b) Sparse Encoder Variant Figure 2. Attention Model Variants: (a) The Decode"
