ICCV,cs_conf,ml_methods,Jin_PixelStitch_Structure-Preserving_Pixel-Wise_Bidirectional_Warps_fo,1,concept|qualitative,1,0,"Our motivation (a) and two-stage bidirectional warped results (b)(c). We zoomed in on a far and a near area to show parallax alignment and the outlines of the stitched images indicate our natural structures. ious ﬁelds, such as medical imaging, panoramic photogra- phy, virtual reality, etc. In practice, image stitching is of- ten confronted with diverse challenging scenes (e.g., large parallax, unnatural distortion, etc), which makes it hard to produce high-quality stitched results. To address these issues, various techniques are intro- duced to traditional feature-based image stitching. On th"
ICCV,cs_conf,ml_methods,Jin_PixelStitch_Structure-Preserving_Pixel-Wise_Bidirectional_Warps_fo,2,overview,0,0,"An overview on PixelStitch. Our framework consists of two stages: global bidirectional alignment and pixel-wise bidirectional warp. In the ﬁrst stage, a homography transformation is estimated and then decomposed to determine the middle plane for the input images. In the second stage, the warped images are used to predict bidirectional ﬂow ﬁelds (F1 and F2), specifying pixel-wise deformation to eliminate residual misalignments and preserve natural structures. 2.1.2. Towards Less Distortion To suppress distortion and obtain more natural panoramas, two categories of methods arose: single-perspect"
ICCV,cs_conf,ml_methods,Jin_PixelStitch_Structure-Preserving_Pixel-Wise_Bidirectional_Warps_fo,3,overview,0,0,"Left: PN-Coef calculation. Right: inverse PN-Coef cal- culation F. The ﬁnal results can be represented by IF 1 = F1 ∗Imid 1 and IF 2 = F2 ∗Imid 2 . In practice, the forward warping process can easily pro- duce invalid holes and meaningless interpolation (e.g., mul- tiple points might be mapped to the same location). To this end, we estimate inverse optical ﬂow ﬁelds (F −1 1 and F −1 2 ) that adopt backward sampling interpolation. 3.2.1. Network Architecture Our network consists of two branches: bidirectional warp- ing ﬁeld estimator and content selection mask generator. Bidirectional Warping F"
