ICML,cs_conf,video,Ske2Grid_Skeleton-to-Grid_Representation_Learning_for_Action_Recogniti,1,comparison,0,0,"Comparison of convolution operations in GCNs and in our Ske2Grid. Graph convolution (top-left) typically convolves every node with their neighboring nodes using speciﬁc kernels. In Ske2Grid, we construct a regular grid patch for skeleton repre- sentation via up-sampling transform (UPT) and graph-node index transform (GIT). Convolution operation upon this grid patch con- volves every grid cell using a shared regular kernel. It operates on a set of grid cells within a squared sub-patch which may be ﬁlled by a set of nodes distributed remotely on the graph, achiev- ing a learnable receptive ﬁeld"
ICML,cs_conf,video,Ske2Grid_Skeleton-to-Grid_Representation_Learning_for_Action_Recogniti,2,overview,1,0,"(a) The overall framework of Ske2Grid: the input skeleton graph with N joints is converted to a grid patch of size H×W using a pair of up-sampling transform (UPT) and graph-node index transform (GIT), which is then fed into the Ske2Grid convolution network for action recognition. (b) Ske2Grid with progressive learning strategy (PLS): the input skeleton is converted to a larger grid patch (H′ >H, W′ >W) using two-stage UPT plus GIT pairs. The well-trained Ske2Grid convolution network for the ﬁrst-stage grid patch as in (a) is re-used to initialize the network for the second-stage grid patch as"
