TPAMI,cs_journal,generative,MIGC_Advanced_Multi-Instance_Generation_Controller_for_Image_Synthesis,1,overview|concept,1,0,"Illustration of MIG. (a) SD generates images from a single image description, struggling with position control (e.g., locating a missing dog) and attribute control (e.g., in- correct hat color) in MIG. (b) MIGC ensures precise attribute and positional fidelity by using bounding boxes for spatial definitions and text for attribute definitions. (c) MIGC++ extends the framework’s versatility, integrating both tex- tual and visual descriptors for attributes and employing bounding boxes and masks to define positions. (d) Building on MIGC and MIGC++, we introduce the Consistent-MIG algorithm to bols"
