TPAMI,cs_journal,video,Weakly_and_Self-Supervised_Class-Agnostic_Motion_Prediction_for_Autono,1,overview|concept,0,0,"Illustration of our weak and self-supervision concept. Outdoor scenes can be decomposed into mobile foreground and static background, which allows us to achieve motion learning with fully or partially annotated FG/BG masks as weak supervision, thereby replacing expensive motion annotations. The motion of foreground points typically occurs in non-ground areas, enabling us to use non-ground/ground masks as an alternative to FG/BG masks to further reduce or even eliminate annotation effort. supervised motion learning. Building on this insight, and lever- aging non-ground/ground cues, we propose t"
TPAMI,cs_journal,video,Weakly_and_Self-Supervised_Class-Agnostic_Motion_Prediction_for_Autono,2,concept,1,0,"Summary of our proposed motion prediction approaches. (a) WeakMotion-FB trains a weakly supervised motion prediction model, WeakMotionNet, by deriving motion supervision from FG/BG points. (b) WeakMotion-NG trains WeakMotionNet by deriving motion supervi- sion from Non-ground/Ground points. (C) SelfMotion-NG trains a self- supervised motion prediction model, SelfMotionNet, by deriving motion supervision from Non-ground/Ground points. 3 PROBLEM FORMULATION OF WEAKLY AND SELF-SUPERVISED MOTION PREDICTION For a sequence of consecutive LiDAR sweeps, following previous works [5], [7], we first sync"
TPAMI,cs_journal,video,Weakly_and_Self-Supervised_Class-Agnostic_Motion_Prediction_for_Autono,3,overview,0,0,"Overview of WeakMotion-FB, a weakly supervised motion prediction approach guided by foreground/background cues. In WeakMotion-FB, we train a motion prediction network, WeakMotionNet, to predict future motion field Xmot,t and FG/BG category map Xfb,t from a sequence of synchronized BEV maps Vt:t−T . To derive motion supervision, we use a pretrained segmentation model (PreSegNet, detailed in Fig. 4) to generate FG/BG points, and apply a Robust Consistency-aware Chamfer Distance loss to these points, enabling self-supervised learning of the motion prediction head. Meanwhile, the auxiliary FG/BG s"
TPAMI,cs_journal,video,Weakly_and_Self-Supervised_Class-Agnostic_Motion_Prediction_for_Autono,4,overview,0,0,"Overview of PreSegNet. Given partially annotated FG/BG masks, we train a foreground/background (FG/BG) segmentation network (PreSegNet), which provides complete per-point FG/BG masks to support the self-supervised motion learning in WeakMotion-FB. simultaneously. Specifically, when fully annotated FG/BG masks are available, PreSegNet can be omitted, and the complete FG/BG labels can be directly used to generate 3D FG/BG points for motion learning. In this section, we first revisit the Chamfer loss in 3D motion tasks (Sec. 4.1) and then discuss the details about our proposed Robust Consistency-"
TPAMI,cs_journal,video,Weakly_and_Self-Supervised_Class-Agnostic_Motion_Prediction_for_Autono,5,unclassified,1,0,"Illustration of confidence estimation. Assuming that an object’s motion remains consistent within a short temporal window, a reliable data point should have forward and backward pseudo motion labels that are equal in magnitude but opposite in direction. Therefore, we measure the confidence of each data point p0(i) based on the consistency be- tween its forward pseudo label yf(i) and backward pseudo label yb(i). (a) A reliable data point with high confidence, where the forward and backward pseudo motion labels are nearly symmetric. (b) An unreliable data point with low confidence, where the for"
TPAMI,cs_journal,video,Weakly_and_Self-Supervised_Class-Agnostic_Motion_Prediction_for_Autono,6,overview,0,0,"Overview of WeakMotion-NG, a weakly supervised motion prediction approach guided by non-ground/ground cues. In WeakMotion-NG, we train a motion prediction network, WeakMotionNet, to predict future motion field Xmot,t and FG/BG category map Xfb,t from a sequence of synchronized BEV maps Vt:t−T . To derive motion supervision, we use an optimization-based plane fitting to generate non-ground/ground points, and apply a Robust Consistency-aware Chamfer Distance loss to these points, enabling self-supervised learning of the motion prediction head. Meanwhile, the auxiliary FG/BG segmentation head is"
TPAMI,cs_journal,video,Weakly_and_Self-Supervised_Class-Agnostic_Motion_Prediction_for_Autono,7,overview,0,0,"Overview of SelfMotion-NG, a self-supervised motion prediction approach guided by non-ground/ground cues. In SelfMotion-NG, we train a motion prediction network, SelfMotionNet, to predict future motion field Xmot,t from a sequence of synchronized BEV maps Vt:t−T . To derive motion supervision, we use an optimization-based plane fitting to generate non-ground/ground points, and apply a Robust Consistency-aware Chamfer Distance loss to these points for self-supervised motion learning. we adopt the same ground segmentation method described in Sec. 5.1.1 to extract ground and non-ground points. We"
TPAMI,cs_journal,video,Weakly_and_Self-Supervised_Class-Agnostic_Motion_Prediction_for_Autono,8,qualitative,0,0,"Qualitative results of motion prediction and foreground/background segmentation predicted by our weakly supervised models (WeakMotionNet) on nuScenes. We show motion with an arrow attached to each cell and represent different categories with different colors. Purple: Foreground; Cyan: Background. Although trained only with foreground/background masks as weak supervision, our models can effectively generate motion and segmentation predictions. Ground Truth Predictions (self-supervised model) Fig. 9. Qualitative results of motion prediction and static/moving segmentation predicted by our self-su"
TPAMI,cs_journal,video,Weakly_and_Self-Supervised_Class-Agnostic_Motion_Prediction_for_Autono,9,qualitative,0,0,"Qualitative results of motion prediction and static/moving segmentation predicted by our self-supervised model (SelfMotionNet) on nuScenes. We show motion with an arrow attached to each cell and represent different motion states with different colors. Orange: Moving objects; Gray: Static objects. Trained without any annotations, our self-supervised model can still achieve reasonable motion prediction. speed groups. In particular, our weakly supervised model trained with only 0.01% annotated FG/BG masks surpasses the fully supervised scene flow models, FlowNet3D and HPLFlowNet, by about 60% on"
