TPAMI,cs_journal,other,W4409017250,3,overview,0,0,"Method overview. Given a query ray from position p ∈R3 in direction v ∈S2, an ellipsoid-based Prior network P uses M ellipsoids {ξi, ri}M i=1 to learn the rough shape of the environment such that it can determine the closest ellipsoid intersected by the ray and predict an SDDF prior. Then, with the intersection point q ∈R3 and ray direction v′ ∈S2 in the ellipsoid’s local frame, a Latent network L generates a latent feature z ∈Rm, which is decoded by the Residual decoder R into residual predictions (δi, δs, δf), i.e., the difference between the ground truth and the prior. Finally, we compose t"
