TIP,cs_journal,perception3d,Balanced_Destruction-Reconstruction_Dynamics_for_Memory-Replay_Class_I,4,comparison|ablation,0,0,"Comparison of the distillation loss at 2-th phase of CwD and AANet w/o and w/ BDR on CIFAR-100 under B = 50, S = 10/5/2. With BDR, the distillation loss will have lower peak values and lower converge values, which means BDR successfully alleviates the degree of maximal destruction and ultimately leads to a higher level of knowledge reconstruction. BDR shows about 9.5% performance gain over CwD [7]. These results demonstrate the generality of BDR and highlight the importance of analyzing the “destruction-reconstruction” dynamics, which is widely overlooked by previous methods. C. The impact of"
