TIP,cs_journal,other,HEOI_Human_Attention_Prediction_in_Natural_Daily_Life_With_Fine-Graine,1,overview|comparison,0,0,"The comparison with mainstream works on the perspectives of attention definition and model architecture. Human attention prediction has been studied for decades in the computer vision domain since the 1990s and many excellent models [3], [9], [11], [12], [13], [14], [15], [16], [17] have remarkably pushed forward its progress. However, the attention definition and model architecture of most works deviate from the essence of attention to a certain degree, ignoring that attention is essentially an interdisciplinary con- cept. Therefore, we argue that attention definition and model architecture s"
TIP,cs_journal,other,HEOI_Human_Attention_Prediction_in_Natural_Daily_Life_With_Fine-Graine,2,overview,0,0,"The overview of our model. The model takes an image I as input and outputs the human attention object A. Our model mainly consists of three modules. The fine-grained HEOI preparation module extracts the environment cue, multi-granularity human cues, and the object cue from the input image. The fine-grained HEOI module explores the relationships among environment, human, and objects through an attention-based network. The Attention object inference module utilizes the features from the last module to predict the attention object. Fig. 3. Human skeleton cue preparation. human box is a rectangle"
TIP,cs_journal,other,HEOI_Human_Attention_Prediction_in_Natural_Daily_Life_With_Fine-Graine,3,unclassified,0,0,"Human skeleton cue preparation. human box is a rectangle box surrounding the overall human. The main step is to locate the upper-left point pl u and the bottom-right point pr b of the human box. Using {(xi,yi)}k i=1 to denote the set of k detected key points, pl u and pr b are calculated as follows: pl u = (min({xi}k i=1), min({yi}k i=1)) (2) pr b = (max({xi}k i=1), max({yi}k i=1)) (3) Based on the calculated pl u and pr b, human box cue Ib is encoded as a binary mask, where pixels inside the box are set as 255 and others are set as 0. human bodypart is defined as the human head rectangle box"
TIP,cs_journal,other,HEOI_Human_Attention_Prediction_in_Natural_Daily_Life_With_Fine-Graine,4,qualitative,0,0,"The qualitative comparisons with baselines. The ground truth attention object is denoted as green box. Predictions are represented by yellow point for Recasens et al. [3], GazeTarget [14] and VSG-IA [72], yellow line for HopeNet [18], and yellow box for Nan et al. [26] and GaTector [27]. Green line and yellow line are also drawn based on ground truth and predictions to visualize the angle error. Fig. 5. The qualitative comparisons with Chong et al. [14] on GOO dataset. The ground truth attention object is denoted as green box. Predictions are represented by yellow box for ours and yellow point"
TIP,cs_journal,other,HEOI_Human_Attention_Prediction_in_Natural_Daily_Life_With_Fine-Graine,5,qualitative|comparison,0,0,"The qualitative comparisons with Chong et al. [14] on GOO dataset. The ground truth attention object is denoted as green box. Predictions are represented by yellow box for ours and yellow point for Chong et al. [14]. Green line and yellow line are also drawn based on ground truth and predictions for visualize the angle error. performance of HEOI based on single-granularity human cue is the worst, however, it still outperforms some baseline meth- ods, indicating our proposed structure is effective. Integrating more human cues results in enhanced model performance, highlighting the effectiveness"
TIP,cs_journal,other,HEOI_Human_Attention_Prediction_in_Natural_Daily_Life_With_Fine-Graine,6,unclassified,0,0,"The prediction results of the models based on different human cues. From upper to lower rows, the results are corresponding to the models based on human box, human bodypart, human skeleton, and all human cues (i.e., box+bodypart+skeleton). The ground truth attention object is denoted as green box, and the predicted attention object is denoted as yellow box. TABLE V THE RESULTS OF MULTI-GRANULARITY HUMAN CUES DIAGNOSIS chalk that is connected with skeleton joint. Meanwhile, the human bodypart is a comprehensive cue, thus it functions well in complex and disturbing situations. As illustrated in"
