TIP,cs_journal,medical,MindGPT_Interpreting_What_You_See_With_Non-Invasive_Brain_Recordings__,6,overview|heatmap,0,0,"Schematic illustration of the semantic reconstruction guided by visual cues. On top of each group, we show the attention map based on the cosine similarity between fMRI and CLIP embedding, and its masking counterpart obtained by thresholding, respectively. can be attributed to the appropriate modeling of visual cues. This is also in line with the character- istics of our human vision system: only a certain part of the rich visual information contained in an image that interests us is perceived by our brain (Chen et al., 2023a). Typically, the [CLS] token’s self-attention weighting coefficient"
TIP,cs_journal,low_level,Degraded_Reference_Image_Quality_Assessment__s2-tip-2023-3234498,1,unclassified,0,0,"In the literature, FR, RR, and NR IQA algorithms are usually tested and at times trained on image databases where each distorted image has undergone a single (often simulated) stage of distortion. This is in clear contrast to real-world visual content distribution scenarios, as illustrated in Fig. 2, where visual content undergoes multiple stages of distortions before reaching its destination. For example, most consumer cameras and camcorders, including mobile phone cameras, store captured content using lossy compression standards such as JPEG and H.264. When these images and videos are upload"
TIP,cs_journal,low_level,Degraded_Reference_Image_Quality_Assessment__s2-tip-2023-3234498,2,overview,0,0,"The framework of practical media distribution systems. In practical media delivery systems, access to pristine reference images in the middle of the delivery chain is either extremely rare or altogether nonexistent. This, cou- pled with the multiple distortion nature of such systems, makes the use of FR and RR IQA infeasible. While NR IQA methods are readily applicable, most NR methods are trained and tested on databases that have images with a single stage of distortion, and their performance lags behind that of FR IQA methods [13]. Efforts have been made recently to design NR IQA methods tha"
TIP,cs_journal,low_level,Degraded_Reference_Image_Quality_Assessment__s2-tip-2023-3234498,3,overview,0,0,"General architectures of DR IQA. Conﬁgurations determined by the statuses of six switches. attempted in the literature. In this paper, we make one of the ﬁrst attempts to establish DR IQA as a new IQA paradigm. We lay out and discuss 53 potential architectures for DR IQA (Section II). We construct two new large-scale synthetically annotated datasets dedicated to DR IQA (Section III-A). We study the behaviors in multiple simultaneous distortions and make some interesting obser- vations not reported before (Section III-B). Based on these observations, we develop novel DR IQA models (Section IV)"
TIP,cs_journal,low_level,Degraded_Reference_Image_Quality_Assessment__s2-tip-2023-3234498,4,overview,0,0,"Since FR methods provide the most reliable quality prediction performance [13] and the PR image is assumed to have perfect quality, to simplify the analysis, we deﬁne IPR Distortion 1 Distortion 2 FR IQA FR IQA DR IQA IFD IDR RSFD ASDR ASFD Fig. 4. Scenario 1: Type-100100 DR IQA architecture. IPR Distortion 1 Distortion 2 FR IQA NR IQA DR IQA IFD IDR RSFD ASDR ASFD Fig. 5. Scenario 2: Type-001100 DR IQA architecture. the absolute scores (AS) of a test image as the FR measure between the test image and its corresponding PR image. In the case of two distortion stages, we may compute the AS score"
TIP,cs_journal,low_level,Degraded_Reference_Image_Quality_Assessment__s2-tip-2023-3234498,5,overview,0,0,"Scenario 2: Type-001100 DR IQA architecture. the absolute scores (AS) of a test image as the FR measure between the test image and its corresponding PR image. In the case of two distortion stages, we may compute the AS scores of the DR and FD images as Eq. 1 and 2: ASDR = FR(IPR, IDR), (1) ASFD = FR(IPR, IFD), (2) respectively, where IPR, IDR, and IFD are the PR, DR and FD images, respectively. The third possible FR comparison is between the DR and FD images, which assesses the quality of the FD image relative to the DR image. Thus, we regard it as the relative score (RS) of the FD image: RSFD"
