IJCV,cs_journal,low_level,Enhancing_HDR_Imaging_with_Joint_Denoising_and_Deblurring__s11263-025-,2,overview,0,0,"The left part shows an overview of the proposed method. The exposure value of LDR frames varies in [−2.0, +2.0]. The short-, medium-, and long-exposure LDR input frames are marked with blue, orange, and yellow lines. The input LDR frames are converted into the HDR domain through “Domain Conversion” and fed into HDR-aware Fusion Module to produce a preliminary HDR feature φH. Then, the HDR feature φH containing remaining noise and motion blur is reﬁned by integrating the superiority of the original LDR frames in the HDR- aware Restoration Module to produce our target HDR output ˜H. The right p"
