IJCV,cs_journal,low_level,Enhancing_HDR_Imaging_with_Joint_Denoising_and_Deblurring__s11263-025-,9,overview|qualitative|comparison,0,0,"Two examples of our proposed online optimization pipeline on real-world mobile datasets. Before the optimization, although the method (trained on our proposed DSLR dataset) maintains its deblur- ring performance on out-domain data, it tends to generate incomplete denoising or over-smooth artifacts in relatively dark or complex textured regions. After the optimization, our method shows satisfying denoising with sharp details while maintaining the deblurring performance 123"
IJCV,cs_journal,low_level,Blind_Image_Deblurring_with_Unknown_Kernel_Size_and_Substantial_Noise_,1,unclassified,0,0,"Given a blurry and potentially also noisy image, how to perform reliable blind image deblurring? The kernel size and the noise type/level are typically unknown, and the image may contain blur or noise only, or both. Left: A street scene captured by a camera mounted on a rapidly moving e-scooter (image captured by Le Peng and Wenjie Zhang of the authors’ group; permission granted); Right: A biological specimen captured by a realistic microscopy system (Image CCDB:3684 from the Cell Image Library; source url: http://cellimagelibrary.org/images/CCDB_3684; created by Mark Ellisman, Gina Sosinsky,"
