IJCV,cs_journal,low_level,Blind_Image_Deblurring_with_Unknown_Kernel_Size_and_Substantial_Noise_,5,comparison,0,0,"Deblurring performance of SelfDeblur [71] and Explore [85] on blurry only (1st row), blurry and noisy (2nd row), and noisy only (3rd row) images. The noise, if present, is Gaussian noise with σ = 0.08. The columns are the observed image (1st column), recovery result of SelfDeblur with exact specification of the kernel size, recovery result of SelfDeblur with over specification of the kernel size, and recovery result of Explore with over specification of the kernel size, respectively. Note that the pretrained models from Explore allow only a fixed kernel size 64 × 64. 3.1 Crucial ingredients 3"
