IJCV,cs_journal,ml_methods,Exemplar-Free_Continual_Learning_of_Vision_Transformers_via_Gated_Clas,6,overview,0,0,"The GCAB distillation mechanism 3.5 GCAB Distillation To overcome the increased computational cost due to multi- ple forward passes for all tasks and the cascaded projection layers, and to remove the memory overhead of our approach, we perform knowledge distillation (Hinton et al., 2015) to transfer the class-conditioned GCAB (the teacher) into a sin- gle class-attention block (CAB) with the same architecture as the GCAB but without masks (student). Moreover, this stu- dent network is an aggregated classiﬁer cAt with the number of logits equal to the overall number of classes observed so far"
