IJCV,cs_journal,perception3d,CT3D_Improving_3D_Object_Detection_with_Keypoint-Induced_Channel-wise_,1,overview,0,0,"General point cloud-based 3D object detection frame- work. We advocate to design flexible architecture with replace- able RPN. source code for our frameworks will be made accessible at https://github.com/hlsheng1/CT3D-plusplus. Keywords 3D object detection · Point clouds · Transformer · Geometric and semantic fusion 1 Introduction 3D object detection is a fundamental technology re- quired for autonomous driving, which plays a vital role in driving decision-making and safety assurance. Many methods Deng et al. (2021); Sheng et al. (2021); Shi et al. (2020a); Yin et al. (2021); Li et al. (2021)"
IJCV,cs_journal,perception3d,CT3D_Improving_3D_Object_Detection_with_Keypoint-Induced_Channel-wise_,2,overview,0,0,"The overall framework of our proposed CT3D framework. First, our CT3D utilizes an arbitrary RPN to generate coarse 3D proposals. Then, the raw points are gathered and processed using the proposed raw-point-based embedding module. Afterwards, the encoded point features are transformed into an effective proposal feature representation by using three-layer standard Transformer encoder and one novel channel-wise decoder. Here, K and V are obtained by linear projection from X. Q and W are learnable parameters. relative coordinates ∆pj i to serve as a more informative representation of the proposal"
